I grew up in Greenfield Indiana a small  hard-working farming community where the  majority of people have the mindset that  you have to be in debt in order to be  successful so when I had the opportunity  to have the Foundation's class in high  school I learned that that's not  necessarily the case you don't have to  go into debt in order to be successful  so this is my classroom where I took the  Foundation's class in high school about  four years ago I sat right over here  where mrs. Graff taught us exactly what  the different principals are so that we  can stay out of debt and one thing that  really hit me was that I could graduate  college debt-free to three months ago  she contacted me by text and she said I  just wanted to let you know that I just  graduated college debt-free  and it was just wonderful to hear that  the kids are behind what they've learned  in my class I did a lot of Pet Sitting  type of jobs I had an account  specifically made that was for college  and I thought almost all of it in there  I went in with leave I had seven  scholarships I applied for fifty-two  while I was in high school and then I  had a couple that waited and they would  only give it to me once I finished my  first year and then that's when we  started kicking in some of our savings  when we talked about how you can go to  college debt-free they again don't  believe that that's not possible I need  to get lots of loans and so it's really  cool to see their faces light up when it  starts to click in and they can see that  oh my gosh  this is reachable I can do this and then  when I get kids that come back and tell  me how successful they've been that's  like the ultimate by taking foundations  in learning those skills and getting  that valuable knowledge I can be  whatever I want to be I don't have to be  restricted to whatever the first job  comes my way I can afford basically to  be choosy so I think it would be really  great and beneficial to all students if  they could be taught foundations class  and really  basically get that foundation of  finances and how to be smart with their  money so that way when they go into  college they can build those habits  there that they can then use in their  life once they get out of college and  continue that streak of seeing debt-free
 

